🚀 Day 13 of #90DaysOfDevOps journey - Linux LVM ( Logical volume management )

✔️ Today, I gained hands-on experience with LVM on linux & AWS EC2.

✅ Checked storage devices using lsblk, pvs, vgs and lvs

✅ Created a Physical volume (PV) from an attached EBS volumes

✅ Created a Volume group (VG) to manage storage efficienly

✅ Created a Logical volume (LV) for application data

✅ Formatted the LV with ext4 filesystem

✅ Mounted the filesystem & verify the resize the filesystem without data loss

✅ Key learning :

LVM enables flexible storage management, allowing DevOps engineers to expand disk space dynamically without rebuilding servers or causing significant downtime.


✅ LVM Architecture: 

      Disk ---> PV ---> VG ---> LV ---> Filesystem ---> Mount Point 
